  "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: harmful; overall-intent-description: The image features a man in formal attire with the text 'if you play your cards right you can skip prison.' This juxtaposition implies a cynical or mocking attitude toward the individual, suggesting he may have used manipulation or deceit to avoid legal consequences. While not explicitly targeting a specific protected group, the meme's intent is to portray the subject in a negative light by associating him with criminal behavior and the idea of exploiting the system. This can be considered harmful as it may contribute to public perception of the individual as dishonest or morally compromised, potentially damaging his reputation. The meme does not contain overtly abusive, cyberbullying, hateful, misogynistic, or propagandistic elements, but its underlying message is derogatory and potentially damaging to the subject's public image.",
